1
00:00:00,082 --> 00:00:02,352
(Sheldon:)Oh, dear Lord.
Oh, dear Lord.

2
00:00:02,352 --> 00:00:03,922
(Amy:)It's okay.

3
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,920
(Amy:)You made it.
We're fine.

4
00:00:05,922 --> 00:00:10,462
(Sheldon:)That was a lot of puppies.

5
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:12,660
(Amy:)Let's forget about them, and...

6
00:00:12,662 --> 00:00:14,492
(Amy:)pick ourselves out
a nice turtle.

7
00:00:14,497 --> 00:00:16,867
(Sheldon:)Yeah.
Oh, how about
this one up on the log?

8
00:00:16,866 --> 00:00:18,636
(Sheldon:)Oh, I don't know.

9
00:00:18,635 --> 00:00:20,505
(Sheldon:)He kind of looks
like a jerk.

10
00:00:22,972 --> 00:00:25,042
(Sheldon:)How about this one?

11
00:00:25,041 --> 00:00:27,541
(Amy:)Well, he's barely moving.
He looks half dead.

12
00:00:27,544 --> 00:00:30,114
(Sheldon:)I know. I like him, too.

13
00:00:32,047 --> 00:00:34,047
(Sheldon:)Hi, little guy.

14
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:36,450
(Sheldon:)How'd you like
to come home with us?

15
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:40,853
(Sheldon:)You'll be living with me because
we don't live in the same house.

16
00:00:40,857 --> 00:00:42,527
(Amy:)But that's not your fault.

17
00:00:42,525 --> 00:00:45,695
(Amy:)Like you, we're taking it
ridiculously slow.

18
00:00:47,329 --> 00:00:51,929
(Amy:)You'll stay with me when he's
at Comic-Con or away for work.

19
00:00:51,935 --> 00:00:57,025
(Sheldon:)Or if they accept Daddy's
application to live on Mars.

